            {
                "entry_id": "53c4ddf6-b593-3f6b-89ca-53044d6be64c",
                "word": "sans-le-sou",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e47e732b-1a45-32c6-9ffc-c992ece35b07",
                        "entry_id": "53c4ddf6-b593-3f6b-89ca-53044d6be64c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne désargentée, très pauvre, mendiant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0dd6878a-f4f8-4f2d-89ff-d7b3c587a504",
                                "sense_id": "e47e732b-1a45-32c6-9ffc-c992ece35b07",
                                "text": "C’est un, une sans-le-sou."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d355beef-d533-40a5-b4db-99587806b62d",
                                "sense_id": "e47e732b-1a45-32c6-9ffc-c992ece35b07",
                                "text": "Le bouquin va de l’avant, le môme a vraiment du sang, et l’on trinque à sa santé dans les cafés du boulevard et les mansardes du Quartier latin. Les sans-le-sou ont reconnu un des leurs, les bohèmes ont vu le gouffre, j’ai sauvé de la fainéantise ou du bagne un tas de garçons qui y couraient, par le sentier que Murger a bordé de lilas !"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b3f025d2-7e34-4183-987b-605117fea230",
                        "source_entry_id": "53c4ddf6-b593-3f6b-89ca-53044d6be64c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e47e732b-1a45-32c6-9ffc-c992ece35b07",
                        "target_lang_word": "Habenichts",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Habenichts",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b91a7160-c699-3ced-b840-3765cee728ba",
                                        "entry_id": "2eafc65f-37ef-34c6-af70-90cf83e59924",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "jemand, der nichts hat/besitzt oder arm ist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "def659b8-b23d-43a3-9ace-66b936bf3ac4",
                                                "sense_id": "b91a7160-c699-3ced-b840-3765cee728ba",
                                                "text": "Nicht alle Diebinnen sind Habenichtse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b6866cc-727e-4b5e-b786-21e60d03e266",
                                                "sense_id": "b91a7160-c699-3ced-b840-3765cee728ba",
                                                "text": "„Was Christa Petrásková meint, ist auch aus anderen Quellen zu erfahren: Sie waren größtenteils Habenichtse.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb0f649b-e769-4f1d-bf00-64445cd2d5a1",
                                                "sense_id": "b91a7160-c699-3ced-b840-3765cee728ba",
                                                "text": "„Freilich würde ich dabei ein doppeltes Risiko eingehen: ungeachtet all seiner Vorzüge ist er doch nur ein hergelaufener Fremdling und Habenichts; wenn ich so einen in meinen Haushalt aufnehme, was bietet Gewähr, daß er mich nicht eines Tages bestiehlt und sich dann heimlich davonmacht?“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0245c3b-99b6-41dd-b800-0611bcaa09e3",
                                                "sense_id": "b91a7160-c699-3ced-b840-3765cee728ba",
                                                "text": "„Beim Souper dankte mir die Pelerinenträgerin dafür, daß ich sie von diesem Habenichts befreit hatte, der sie belästigte und immer mit den Worten erschreckte, er werde sich umbringen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c32d50fe-99b1-419b-bdb8-2e54646b8cf7",
                                                "sense_id": "b91a7160-c699-3ced-b840-3765cee728ba",
                                                "text": "„Indiens Ablehnung des Atomsperrvertrags, der die Hegemonie der Nuklearmächte festschreibt und die nuklearen Habenichtse auf die Dauer zu Staaten zweiter Klasse degradiert, entsprach ebenfalls seinem Anspruch auf eine solche Weltgeltung.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a9e9119a-c3a5-4feb-b02b-3357a537cf45",
                        "source_entry_id": "53c4ddf6-b593-3f6b-89ca-53044d6be64c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e47e732b-1a45-32c6-9ffc-c992ece35b07",
                        "target_lang_word": "penniless",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "penniless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a623a4bd-8554-3ae1-bdcb-fce39a6467cc",
                                        "entry_id": "88576137-0ea4-3599-b1cf-ebed817e912c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lacking even the smallest amount of money."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdd7f340-8960-4405-a210-cb343c4f16c9",
                                                "sense_id": "a623a4bd-8554-3ae1-bdcb-fce39a6467cc",
                                                "text": "In societies without national insurance of any kind, almshouses are the last refuge of penniless people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a640b167-c15d-4fc7-88f0-fe6fe03e1d33",
                                                "sense_id": "a623a4bd-8554-3ae1-bdcb-fce39a6467cc",
                                                "text": "In a functioning digital economy, being cashless is far different from being penniless, because cash is merely one form of money; but some preppers hoard gold in case the system gets destroyed and cashlessness suddenly becomes pennilessness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12e84425-26ff-4e48-a0fb-2d60186ae399",
                                                "sense_id": "a623a4bd-8554-3ae1-bdcb-fce39a6467cc",
                                                "text": "A dollar and a quarter seems a small sum, but if you are absolutely penniless it might as well be a thousand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4925aadb-5aa2-493d-acbf-4682e461618e",
                                                "sense_id": "a623a4bd-8554-3ae1-bdcb-fce39a6467cc",
                                                "text": "This time was most dreadful for Lilian. Thrown on her own resources and almost penniless, she maintained herself and paid the rent of a wretched room near the hospital by working as a charwoman, sempstress, anything. In a moment she had dropped to the level of a casual labourer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26f3721d-9d1e-3c58-baf5-5841db400a0c",
                                        "entry_id": "88576137-0ea4-3599-b1cf-ebed817e912c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Abstaining from the use of penny coins, despite having fully decimalized currency, via rounding of cash transactions (but not necessarily of cashless ones)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f5485cc-bf3a-4480-9f7f-7fe212974aed",
                                                "sense_id": "26f3721d-9d1e-3c58-baf5-5841db400a0c",
                                                "text": "Canada became a penniless country in 2013 simply by rounding its cash transactions to the nearest nickel but otherwise not changing anything."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "368674d9-c38a-4d39-8e2b-49b952a7dd77",
                        "source_entry_id": "53c4ddf6-b593-3f6b-89ca-53044d6be64c",
                        "source_sense_id": "e47e732b-1a45-32c6-9ffc-c992ece35b07",
